  "summary": "CGI::Carp versions before 5.00 for Perl leak warnings across requests in persistent environments via the…",
  "details": "CGI::Carp versions before 5.00 for Perl leak warnings across requests in persistent environments via the warningsToBrowser buffer.\n\nWarnings are held in a package-level buffer until warningsToBrowser writes them into the page as HTML comments, and the buffer is never cleared between requests. Under mod_perl, FastCGI or PSGI, warnings from one request are written into a later one.\n\nWarnings that contain one user's request data can appear in the HTML sent to another user.",
  "severity": [
